From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:45:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 85/88] test: add feature_p2mr_rescue.py and
 feature_p2mr_rescue_signet.py

On regtest, with the rescue proofs made as the test runs: the activation
boundary in blocks and in the mempool, through sendrawtransaction,
testmempoolaccept and packages; the policy check before the trigger and
after a reorganization over it; removal below the lane's height with the
checks disabled and working; one to four inputs; spends outside the
template; the P2P gate with and without wtxid relay, orphans, repeated
sends and the -whitelist directions; the logs and gettripwireinfo, the
log only for template R1, and a block whose input drops 998 tokens and
has 50,000 key-sized pushes in a branch never run connecting within a
minute without a log line, nor an R1-shaped spend on a regtest with P2MR
later than the lane; a parent put back from a disconnected block with a
rescue child and that child's own child in the mempool: with the lane
kept open all three stay, their dependency edges and ancestor and
descendant counts restored, and once the lane closes the parent stays,
the rescue child goes by the filter and its child as a descendant; a
rescue record that no rescue check reads (an OP_TRUE leaf, relayed by a
node with -acceptnonstdtxn), which below H4R only the filter removes; a
reorganization across H3;
restarts, -reindex, -reindex-chainstate, VerifyDB level 4 and pruning;
and the hard fork, with an M4-S build as the late node when
M4S_BITCOIND names its bitcoind, or this build with the lane never open.

On a custom signet with -signetrescue: the network id of the challenge,
a proof for regtest's refused, and the options.
